name: belief-revision
kind: inferred
shape: categorical
face: in
membrane: false
note: a belief previously held as true was measured false — the commit
      names the falsified claim in quotes and the observation that killed
      it. Distinct from defect (the belief was about behavior, not code)
      and from design (no new shape was chosen; an old fact was revoked).
      The signal exists so "we thought X was true" has a discoverable
      correction point later.
